crine hypercalcemia.", "Elevated ALP without osteolytic features provides moderate support for malignancy with bone involvement but less than definitive.", "Normal bone disease history with elevated ALP moderately disfavors endocrine hypercalcemia while supporting malignancy/reactive causes."], "unresolved_questions": [], "askable_discriminators": ["History of calcium-containing antacid overuse", "Known parathyroid disease", "Recent vitamin D supplementation"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Serum PTH level", "25-hydroxyvitamin D test", "Parathyroid imaging"]}, "target_level": 2}
